<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhadamistus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 58 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhadamistus was an Iberian prince, son of King Pharasmanes I, who seized the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> in 51 CE after treacherously killing his uncle Mithridates, its Roman-backed king. His rule was challenged by the Parthian candidate Tiridates, and he was driven out within a few years and later put to death by his father. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, he threw his pregnant wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenobia">Zenobia</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a> during his flight, though she survived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhadamistus.jpg" alt="Rhadamistus" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Alberi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhadamistus,_by_Francesco_Alberi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
